class GridTools {
    /** Swaps row r1 and row r2 of m. */
    public static void swapRows(int[][] m, int r1, int r2) {
        /* missing code */
    }
}
```

options.text:
```
int[] temp = m[r1];
m[r1] = m[r2];
m[r2] = temp;
```

```
for (int c = 0; c < m[r1].length; c++) {
    m[r1][c] = m[r2][c];
}
```

payload.explanation_en:
The correct answer is:
```
int[] temp = m[r1];
m[r1] = m[r2];
m[r2] = temp;
```
A 2D array holds row references, so swapping the references with a temporary variable swaps the rows.
An incorrect option:
```
m[r1] = m[r2];
m[r2] = m[r1];
```
Both rows end up referring to the old row r2; the old row r1 is lost.
An incorrect option:
```
int t = m[r1][0];
m[r1][0] = m[r2][0];
m[r2][0] = t;
```
Swaps only the first elements of the two rows.
An incorrect option:
```
for (int c = 0; c < m[r1].length; c++) {
    m[r1][c] = m[r2][c];
}
```
Copies row r2 into row r1 but never copies row r1 into row r2.

