payload.explanation_en:
The correct answer is:
```
while (total + next <= limit) {
    total += next;
    next++;
}
return next - 1;
```
The condition must test total + next so the limit is not exceeded, and next - 1 is the number of terms added.
An incorrect option:
```
while (total + next < limit) {
    total += next;
    next++;
}
return next - 1;
```
Stops when the total would equal limit, which is still allowed.
An incorrect option:
```
while (total <= limit) {
    total += next;
    next++;
}
return next - 1;
```
Adds one term after the total has already reached the limit, so the total can exceed it.
An incorrect option:
```
while (total + next <= limit) {
    total += next;
    next++;
}
return next;
```
Returns the next number to add instead of the count of numbers added.

